  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 BGC tracers are stored per unit volume, so converting DIC and total alkalinity to micromoles per kilogram requires density and affects every mean and bias.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `dissic`/`talk` are mol m-3: convert every cell before averaging, µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ, with ρ the in-situ density from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` (`ref_pressure=None`); `transform_unit`'s constant default (mean surface density) errs by about a per cent in the deep ocean, and the required µmol/kg basis makes the conversion mandatory.",
        "Record the density used (`attrs['density_assumption']`); the `chl`/`dfe` factors and the inventory/concentration-to-content advice do not apply here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-carbonate-system-definitions",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-carbonate-system-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "21e66b2c314b75cf7dc1686ccf50982ccd163493b1761b789634d05c433243bd",
      "reason": "This fixes what dissic, talk and pH mean, including that pH is total scale, so the comparison with GLODAP TCO2, TAlk and pH is defined correctly.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compare model `ph` (total scale, in situ) only with GLODAP `pHtsinsitutp`, not `pHts25p0`.",
        "If the pH result leans on CESM2's carbonate constants, state that the CESM2 paper does not document them (unverified assumption)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "All bias, RMSE, correlation and depth-profile averages must use only cells where the model and GLODAP are both valid, and model ranking must use a common mask.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all sources on the GLODAP 1° grid and take the DIC bias/RMSE/correlation on one mask from `build_comparison_mask` with `ocean_only=False` (the reference is not WOA23), applied by `.where(mask)`; report the cell counts and each model's `mean_data`/`mean_reference` next to the bias.",
        "Also report that the per-source 0-50 m global means each cover that source's own cells, so their model-minus-GLODAP difference is not the shared-mask bias."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The 2002 minus 1971-2000 DIC change is a baseline-dependent anomaly, and its ratio to the GLODAP bias must be interpreted as a change-versus-bias comparison rather than a direct error.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no anomaly, climate index, event detection or DJF-vs-JFM seasonal aggregation is involved; 2002 minus the 1971-2000 mean is a plain difference of two means of the same source, so no climatology baseline convention arises."
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global means over 0-50 m must be area- or volume-weighted, not simple unweighted averages over cells or levels.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use `compute_basic_stat` with `op='volume_weighted_mean'` for any mean spanning depth (the 0-50 m means) and `op='area_weighted_mean'` for horizontal ones, weights restricted to the same valid (NaN-free) cells; unweighted `mean()` over (y, x) or over latitude is wrong.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the map's spatial correlation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Integrals and masks should be computed on the native grids, with regridding used only for the map and pattern comparisons against GLODAP.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute each source's global means and its 2002-minus-1971-2000 change on its own native grid with its own weights; regrid (`regrid_horizontal`, 'conservative') only for the map comparison and state which numbers come from which grid.",
        "Bias at 0, 100, 500, 1000, 2000 m: interpolate every product to those depths with `regrid_vertical`, never select the nearest level."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "areacello and volcello provide the cell areas, volumes and layer thicknesses needed for 0-50 m vertical averaging and global weighting.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Weight with each model's own `areacello`/`volcello`; the 0-50 m thickness is `volcello`/`areacello` (`cell_thickness_like`), since `thkcello`/`masscello`/`rhozero` are absent and `lev_bnds` differences fail at partial bottom cells.",
        "GFDL-ESM4's `volcello` varies in time (the loader handles it); report `attrs['area_source']` and `attrs['volume_source']`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "CMIP6 salinity is Practical Salinity with a 0.001 scale factor, which must be handled correctly when computing density for the micromoles-per-kilogram conversion.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` holds practical-salinity numbers (order 35) despite the units string \"0.001\" — never rescale it; convert S_P to S_A with the location-dependent gsw function before using it in density or other TEOS-10 routines, otherwise the density used for the µmol/kg conversion is biased."
      ]
    }
